  "description": "Years of production: 2020-2023\n\nSucceeded by the Jeht Gen2. See the current Jeht.\n\nThe first generation Jeht was our genre-defying, do-everything 140mm 29er steel full suspension bike. A quiver killer and the Swiss army knife of the droplink range: if you needed one bike to do all your mountain biking, this was it. 140mm of rear travel paired with a 150mm fork on trail-taming 29\" wheels gave a bike with a spring in its step that always had your back.\n\nIt spliced the accurate handling of the FlareMAX with a solid dose of RocketMAX speed. The bespoke Reynolds 853 mainframe with Longshot geometry was just as happy zipping round a trail centre as swishing along alpine singletrack or over Lake District passes. Riders could also run it as a mullet, with a 27.5\" rear wheel, for a lower BB, more standover and a more playful ride.\n\nFinishes: UK-made Launch Edition in Afterburner and Matte Teal; Taiwan-made production frames in Nimbus and Midnight Blue; and a final one-off run in Dark Crystal Malt.\nSizes: Small, Medium, Large and XL. Wheels: 29\", or 29\" front / 27.5\" rear mullet. Rear travel: 140mm.",
